/*
test import and linked files.
this is a SECOND library header, imported alongside library.slh.

its job is the completer-side export rule: an incomplete class's completer
exports its layout as link-time absolute symbols, so a completion whose
hidden fields embed ANOTHER module's incomplete (or computed-layout) class
cannot fold them and must be rejected. that rejection needs two modules to
exist at all, which is why this header does.
*/

/*
claude says:

BadPack declares NO methods and NO hooks on purpose: its completion exists only
inside extra.sl's negative blocks, so in the live build it stays forever open —
a declared member would be a symbol no source ever defines. Its only job is to
be the class those negatives try (and fail) to complete; it is never
instantiated. (The same never-instantiated pattern as library.slh's NoCtor.)
*/

/* incomplete class, completed only by the negative cases in extra.sl */
BadPack(...) { }
